1. What this covers. This licence covers the files in any folder named "ee" in
this repository (the "Enterprise Code"). The rest of the repository is licensed
under the Apache License 2.0; see LICENSE at the root. Third-party components
keep the licences their owners chose.

2. Free use. Without paying, you may read, copy, run and modify the Enterprise
Code for:

  - development and testing;
  - evaluating PipesHub; and
  - building and showing a prototype, including one built for a client.

None of these may be production use. PipesHub provides a licence key for these
uses free of charge where one is needed to turn features on; its limits are set
by the key.

3. Production use. "Production use" means using the Enterprise Code with an
organisation's real data for its day-to-day work. It is production use once
people outside the team building or evaluating the installation rely on it for
their work. A development, test or demonstration installation is not
production use, even when it holds a copy of real data. Production use needs a
valid PipesHub licence key for that installation, obtained under PipesHub's
subscription terms or another written agreement with PipesHub. You must stay
within the key's limits: the installation and web address it names, its
features, its seats and its term.

4. The licence key. You may not:

  - remove, disable, change or work around the licence check;
  - enable a feature the key does not cover; or
  - copy Enterprise Code outside an "ee" folder, or into another product, to
    avoid the key.

5. Your changes. You may change the Enterprise Code and publish patches to it.
PipesHub and its licensors keep all rights in the Enterprise Code and in any
changes you make to it. Changed Enterprise Code may be used in production only
under a valid licence key, like the code it changes.

6. Sharing. You may share the Enterprise Code, changed or not, only:

  - as part of a copy or fork of this repository that keeps this licence, the
    notices and the licence check intact; or
  - with a client for whom you are building a prototype under section 2.

You may not sell or sublicense the Enterprise Code, or offer it to others as a
hosted service, except under a written agreement with PipesHub, such as the
partner programme.

7. Notices. Every copy must keep this licence and the copyright notices.

8. Contributions. Contributions to Enterprise Code are accepted on the terms in
CONTRIBUTING.md.

9. Ending. If you break this licence, your rights under it end. If PipesHub
tells you of a breach and you stop within 30 days, your rights continue, but
only the first time. This second chance does not apply to removing, disabling
or working around the licence check on purpose (section 4).

10. No warranty. The Enterprise Code is provided "as is", without warranty of
any kind. PipesHub is not liable for any claim or damage arising from it, to
the extent the law allows.

11. Trademarks. This licence grants no right to use PipesHub's names or logos.
